        <li>
          <title>Objective</title>    
          <p>
            In this activity, we'll explore the special limit <md>
              \lim_{x\rightarrow 0} \frac{\sin(x)}{x} = 1
            </md> using the area of the unit circle.
          </p>
          </li>
          <li> <title>Helpful Fact</title>
            <p>
              There is a formula for the area of a triangle when you know two adjacent sides and the angle between them:
            </p>
          </li>
          </ul>
          </p>
  </introduction>

