<sidebyside>
<exercise>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      We can try to approximate this area by cutting the circle into triangles. This diagram cuts the unit circle into four triangles and then pulls one of the triangles out independently. For this partition of the circle: </p>
  </introduction>
  <task>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Find the angle <m>\theta</m>.
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
  <task>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Find the area of one of the triangles.
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
  <task>
    <statement>
      <p>
        Find the total area of all 4 triangles put together.
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
</exercise>

